[Answer format]
2025-05-01 00:46:10 - Thread-79 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• “publication_number” (PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS) : unique patent publication identifier – will be returned to user.  
• “grant_date” (PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS)          : allows us to keep only patents granted from 2010‑01‑01 through 2018‑12‑31.  
• “citation” (PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS)             : JSON/VARIANT array that lists each backward/forward citation; we will FLATTEN it and look inside each element.  
      – Inside every element there is usually a key such as “category” (sometimes called “type”) whose value may be “SEA” (= Search Examiner‑added backward citation).  
• (no other tables are strictly needed, so only PUBLICATIONS is used).  

Typical conditions that may be useful  
1. p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231  
2. c.value:"category"::STRING = 'SEA'      -- while exploring we may use ILIKE '%SEA%' first.  
3. GROUP BY p."publication_number" to count how many SEA citations each patent has.  

Ten inspection / exploration SQLs (every query limited to 20 rows, all column names in double quotes).  

```sql
-- Description: Look at a handful of granted publications in 2010‑2018 together with their raw “citation” array
SELECT p."publication_number",
       p."grant_date",
       p."citation"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p
WHERE  p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Flatten the citation array for one publication to inspect the structure of each element
SELECT p."publication_number",
       f.value                                                    AS "citation_element"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
WHERE  p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
  AND  p."publication_number" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Extract the “category” (or similar key) from each citation element to see possible values
SELECT p."publication_number",
       f.value:"category"::STRING         AS "citation_category",
       f.value:"type"::STRING             AS "citation_type",
       f.value:"publication_number"::STRING AS "cited_pubno"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
WHERE  p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Show distinct citation categories that occur in 2010‑2018 data (helps confirm 'SEA' label)
SELECT DISTINCT f.value:"category"::STRING AS "distinct_category"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
WHERE  p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Count citations of every category per publication (first step before filtering ‘SEA’)
SELECT p."publication_number",
       f.value:"category"::STRING  AS "citation_category",
       COUNT(*)                    AS "n_citations"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
WHERE  p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
GROUP  BY p."publication_number", f.value:"category"::STRING
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Show only SEA‑category citations per publication (no aggregation yet)
SELECT p."publication_number",
       f.value:"category"::STRING AS "citation_category",
       f.value:"publication_number"::STRING AS "cited_pubno"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
WHERE  p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
  AND  f.value:"category"::STRING = 'SEA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Count number of SEA backward citations for each publication from 2010‑2018
SELECT p."publication_number",
       COUNT(*)  AS "sea_citation_count"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
WHERE  p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
  AND  f.value:"category"::STRING = 'SEA'
GROUP  BY p."publication_number"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Same as above but order by count descending to see patents with the most SEA citations
SELECT p."publication_number",
       COUNT(*) AS "sea_citation_count"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
WHERE  p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
  AND  f.value:"category"::STRING = 'SEA'
GROUP  BY p."publication_number"
ORDER  BY "sea_citation_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Use DISTINCT to ensure each cited publication is tallied only once per citing patent (if needed)
SELECT p."publication_number",
       COUNT( DISTINCT f.value:"publication_number"::STRING ) AS "unique_sea_citations"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
WHERE  p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
  AND  f.value:"category"::STRING = 'SEA'
GROUP  BY p."publication_number"
ORDER  BY "unique_sea_citations" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: Final concise query delivering publication number and number of SEA backward citations (2010‑2018)
SELECT p."publication_number",
       COUNT(*) AS "sea_backward_citations"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
WHERE  p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231          -- granted 2010‑2018
  AND  f.value:"category"::STRING = 'SEA'                    -- SEA category only
GROUP  BY p."publication_number"
ORDER  BY p."publication_number"
LIMIT 20;
```

